# Settings the engine reads from your environment. You will likely never need one: every reel, on every
# route, builds with none of them set.
#
# The engine does not load this file by itself. To use a line, set it where your terminal picks it up: on a
# Mac, an `export NAME=value` line in ~/.zprofile; in Git Bash on Windows, the same line in ~/.bashrc.
#
# Instagram research (reference-reel) has no line here. Apify is a connector you add in Claude with
# `/mcp` (https://mcp.apify.com), signed in with your own Apify key.

# The speech tools on Apple Silicon Macs and Windows: point at a folder that already holds them.
# Unset, the rough cut builds them once in ~/.cache/reels-editing-engine/whisperx-venv.
# REELS_ENGINE_WHISPERX_VENV=

# The same for the Intel Mac route, which uses a lighter set of speech tools.
# Unset: ~/.cache/reels-editing-engine/fasterwhisper-venv.
# REELS_ENGINE_NOFW_VENV=

# Where the upload-ready copy of a finished reel or carousel lands. Unset: your Downloads folder.
# REELS_EXPORT_DIR=
